dialogue trust_engineer_1
title: The list of questions
trigger: Trust engineer level=1
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The wagon is jacked up on two stones, and a lamp hangs from the axle. The Engineer lies underneath with a stub of pencil, writing in a grease-black notebook instead of turning the wrench.
  * The axle won't fix itself while you write about it. -> axle
    do: AddTrust $with -2
  * Is that the list you promised me back in the red? -> list
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * Need a hand under there? -> hand
    do: AddTrust $with 4

node axle hero
  The axle's done. Has been for an hour. I'm under here because it's the only quiet spot in this camp, and because I'm writing about you.
  -> pages

node list hero
  You remembered. The Choir never remembered anything I said past the price. Yes. It's the list. It's getting long.
  -> pages

node hand hero
  Hold the lamp still, that'll do. Not there. There. Good. Now I can see what I've written about you.
  -> pages

node pages commander
  The Engineer rolls out on a sack and holds the notebook up to the lamp. Page after page, every line ends in a question mark.
  -> questions

node questions hero
  Question one. Why does it hum near you and nowhere else. Question two. Why does it go quiet at nine paces and not ten. Question three. Why does the needle on my gauge swing toward you when you walk past, like you're a tap.
  -> tap

node tap hero
  In the Underspire I kept a tap running. Tap Seven, under the old fish market. Halcyon pipe, older than anyone's grandmother. Nobody knew what it was pulling, and nobody asked, because it kept the lights on.
  -> needle

node needle hero
  Then I come up into the red, and a Halcyon orb wakes up for a stranger in a white wagon. And my needle swings the same way it used to swing at Tap Seven. I'd like to know why, Commander.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Engineer looks at the satchel where the orb rides, then back at the Commander, and waits.
  * Take it. Open it up, carefully, and tell me what you find. -> lent
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag engineer:orb_lent
  * Measure it all you like. But it stays shut, and it stays with me. -> watched
    do: AddTrust $with 5
    do: SetFlag engineer:orb_watched
  * No. That orb is the only reason any of us are still alive. Leave it be. -> refused
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag engineer:orb_refused

node lent hero
  You're handing it to me. Just like that. Nobody hands me the good parts. I'll go slow, and I'll put every screw back where it came out, and I'll tell you everything, even the parts that don't make sense.
  -> close_line

node watched hero
  Fair. I'd do the same with a part I couldn't replace. I'll bring the gauge to you, then. You'll be the most measured commander in the red.
  -> close_line

node refused hero
  It's not alive because nobody looked inside it, Commander. It's alive because of you. That's the bit I'm trying to understand. But fine. I'll write that down too.
  -> close_line

node close_line hero
  Go on, I'll lower the wagon. Question four can wait till morning. Question four is a big one.
  -> close

node close commander
  The jack creaks, the wagon settles onto the new axle, and the lamp swings once and goes still. The notebook goes into the Engineer's coat, a pencil tucked through the spine.
